From: Jinbo Zhang <jinboz1@uci.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:24:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] TrackMLReader: deterministic event split from id lists

The reader split events with an unseeded random_split over a list whose
order came from glob, so train/val/test differed between runs and machines.

New config option `split_lists: {trainset: ids.txt, valset: ..., testset: ...}`
takes each set from a text file of event ids (one per line, '#' comments),
e.g. the frozen lists written from the gd manifest. Listed events without
all four input files raise, overlapping lists raise, and unknown keys
raise. Without split_lists, complete events are sorted by id and split
80/10/10 with a generator seeded by `split_seed` (default 0).

gd-displaced patch 0006 (plan item f).
